processed_intake_routes:
  docs_manifest: docs/report-intake/2026-07-01/MANIFEST.md
  docs_synthesis: docs/report-intake/2026-07-01/minimodel-p2p-report-synthesis-2026-07-01.md
  durable_roadmap: wiki/runtime-mirust/research/minimodel-p2p-tiny-model-exchange-roadmap-2026-07-01.md
  manifest_verifier_mvp: wiki/runtime-mirust/research/minimodel-manifest-verifier-mvp-2026-07-01.md
  minimodel_site_roadmap: E:\Source\Rust\MiniModel.org\ROADMAP.md
  source_site_result: processed source-site copies removed from agent-file-handoff/Improvement/ after byte-exact preservation and pointer updates.
roadmap_guardrails:
  - Rust-first P2P model exchange architecture; evaluate Pear/Bare/Hyper as tradeoffs, not core SLMComposer dependencies.
  - Legal/liability boundaries must keep MiniModel.org as metadata/catalog guidance until legal review; no claims that third-party models are safe, legal, or endorsed.
  - Secure manifests must be checksum-bound and route source identity, model cards, license, tokenizer/config, eval/admission evidence, chunk/Merkle data, and signatures.
  - Tiny-model creation/import stays tied to TinyRustLM local review, conversion, validation, runtime-smoke, eval, admission, and local import receipts.
  - Project servers never run user model bytes and never serve user model bytes.
next_implementation_slice:
  - Stabilize the `key=value` manifest parser and duplicate-key rejection.
  - Reject project-server model-byte URLs and server-side execution claims before artifact checks.
  - Verify a user-supplied local `.slm` byte count and SHA256 before any SLMComposer handoff.
  - Write a local import receipt with manifest checksum, artifact checksum, validation result, and `user-selected-slmcomposer-local-file-open` next gate.
  - Keep peer transfer, DHTs, relays, and desktop UI out of the first verifier slice.
success_criteria:
  - Active intake buckets remain empty or placeholder-only.
  - SLMComposer.com remains browser-local and user-selected local `.slm` import remains the model byte boundary.
  - MiniModel.org implementation work starts with local schema parsing, verifier checks, and receipt writing; metadata-only catalog and peer transfer remain later phases.
  - Long-term memory remains pointer-based and checksum-bearing.
  - Before claiming completion, run relevant pointer audits and `git diff --check`.
